# Rendered by fleet-init from fleet.env. Source on the mac venue.
# Two Android devices are attached at a time; the venue has three and swaps them.
# Currently connected (2026-09-17), both over USB so the transport name IS the serial:
#
#   9b010059305330363400f1f217fa8c  Xiaomi 25028RN03Y  720x1640   2.7 GB   Android 15
#   HA26QKR0                        Lenovo TB520FU     1840x2944  14.9 GB  Android 16
#
# The Xiaomi is FIRST, so ANDROID_SERIAL and every unqualified run land on a PHONE,
# which is the form factor most checks assume. The cost is that the default is also
# the venue's most memory-constrained device: an unexplained OOM or kill on a default
# run is a reason to re-run claiming HA26QKR0, not necessarily a defect.
#
# Claim by serial when the device is the point:
#   9b010059305330363400f1f217fa8c  LOW MEMORY (2.7 GB). A `web` page's real cost lives
#                                   in a separate Chromium renderer the app's VmRSS
#                                   never sees, so a budget that merely survives at
#                                   5 GB fails here -- this device FALSIFIED #153's
#                                   memory ceiling (see #244) rather than confirming it.
#   HA26QKR0                        The only Android TABLET form factor, and the high-
#                                   memory end (14.9 GB): use it for layout-shaped
#                                   checks and to show a ceiling does not trip spuriously.
#
# Swapped out for now: Samsung SM-G990B (RFCRC0FY4ZJ, 5.2 GB, Android 16). Its 0/1/2
# runtime profile is already recorded in #230. Put it back as the default once the
# live-runtime budget work (#230/#244) has landed -- a mid-range phone is the better
# everyday default than either extreme.
export FLEET_ANDROID_SERIALS="9b010059305330363400f1f217fa8c HA26QKR0"
# iPad Air 13-inch (M2) sim, physical iPad Air (4th gen), iPhone 16 Pro sim,
# iPad Air 13-inch (M3) sim (iOS 18.4), iPad Air 11-inch (M2) sim, iPhone 16 Pro sim
# (iOS 18.4) as a SECOND phone: the list had four iPad-class devices and one phone, so
# issue 87 — a check that is about an iPhone's width and cannot substitute an iPad —
# sat in a claim-retry loop while four devices it could not use were free.
# The two extra iPads are here because iPad coverage was the scarce one: with four
# agents in flight, issue 112's run found "the two iPads were claimed by other runs"
# and fell back to the iPhone, which is the wrong form factor for a layout check.
# Order matters: the first is what a run takes when it picks no UDID of its own.
export FLEET_IOS_UDIDS="A42682BF-67BA-48CC-875F-B47E31F191FF 5E8DA01B-5B74-5EFB-B9B1-42E9C4707FAB 40696C9C-F8EE-483F-83FF-AFA89CCC5FE7 60F8C0FE-6BC3-4C1A-831E-9678B8B21F8E B8C06040-12CE-4E8D-B43A-53AE3A7B403C 4D2F2641-B0A3-4B55-BF5C-3166299F579A"
export ANDROID_SERIAL="${FLEET_ANDROID_SERIALS%% *}"
